{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Encapsulation and Trends in OOP"}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear or use to talk about Encapsulation and Trends in OOP."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Modal can for ability and possibility review, e.g., Software developers can create organized libraries and other programmers can use them.  Singular and plural of countable nouns, e.g., library - libraries, specification - specifications, capability - capabilities, ability - abilities."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Participates in simple conversations or simulated situations about the communicative topics for this level through the appropriate use of simple pronunciation aspects, and grammar and vocabulary structures. Recognizes simple ideas on requirement reports, tools for Object Oriented Programming, and other basic progamming tools."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n3le02ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Modal can for ability and possibility"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Modal verbs are auxiliary verbs, which need another verb to function. There are three verbs that you can use to express possibility or ability. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The modal verbs to talk about possibility or ability are <span class=\"strong\"> can </span> , <span class=\"strong\"> be able to </span> , and <span class=\"strong\">could. </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "There are different trends and details about encapsulation that we can use taking into account encapsulation as one fundamental OOP concept."}, {"type": "example", "content": "By using encapsulation, designers are able to promote the development of programs with reliability."}, {"type": "example", "content": "In this way we could create more readable programs. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use these modal verbs in the affirmative form like this:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\">Subject +<span class=\"strong\"> modal verb</span> + <span class=\"strong\">main verb</span> + complement.</div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Be able to</span>  needs to modify the verb <span class=\"strong\">to be</span>  according to the subject. (am not, isn't, aren't)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember the main uses for these modal verbs:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"CAN\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Express ability or show ability.</br> To suggest a possibility or give an option</br>. To ask for or to give permission (informal). </br> To show impossibility (can't).</br> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"BE ABLE TO\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We use it to talk about ability, possibility and capability.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"COULD\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"To show past ability (past of the verb can). </br>  To ask a polite question.</br> To use a more formal way than with can.</br>  To suggest a possibility/opportunity or give an option.</br>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Singular and Plural of Countable Nouns"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Countable nouns are the ones that you can use numbers to count instead of a different measurement unit; they are individual things, they can be singular or plural. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">countable nouns </span> with a/an, and with numbers and other determiners (quantifiers, demonstratives, articles, possessive adjectives).  "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Quatifiers\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Demostratives\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Articles\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Possessive adjectives\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"few, some, many \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"this, these, those, that \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the, a, an \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"my, your , his, her, our, their, its. \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For the plural form of most nouns, add  <span class=\"strong\">s</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "pencil \u2013 pencil<span class=\"strong\">s</span>.</br> desk \u2013 desk<span class=\"strong\">s</span>.</br> program \u2013 program<span class=\"strong\">s</span>.</br>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For nouns that end in <i> ch</i>, <i>x</i>, <i>s</i>, or <i>s</i> sounds, add <span class=\"strong\">es</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "box \u2013 box<span class=\"strong\">es</span>.</br> watch \u2013 watch<span class=\"strong\">es</span>.</br> bus \u2013 bus<span class=\"strong\">es</span>.</br>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For nouns ending in <i>f</i> or <i> fe</i>, change <span class=\"strong\">f </span> to <span class=\"strong\">v </span> and add <span class=\"strong\">es</span>.</br>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "wolf \u2013 wolv<span class=\"strong\">es</span>.</br> leaf \u2013 leav<span class=\"strong\">es</span>.</br> life \u2013 live<span class=\"strong\">s</span>.</br>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "promote"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "to encourage people to, use, do, or support something"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: By using encapsulation, designers are able to promote the development of programs with reliability."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le02ob08aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "reliability"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "applied to objects, a person or an idea capable of being relied on"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: By using encapsulation, designers are able to promote the development of programs with reliability. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le02ob08aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fad"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "critics to a style, activity, or interest that is very popular for a short period of time "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We know that OOP trends have been fad by other programmers judging its capabilities and effectiveness by the implementation of Smalltalk."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le02ob08aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "wiki "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a website that allows users to add, delete, and edit the content, or the information of a website. "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We can use the benefits of the Internet for internal communication and collaboration in the office simple processes such as a blog or wikis that can benefit employees and customers' knowledge and keep everyone updated."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le02ob08aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Environmentally conscious  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "been worried about the eco system to keep it safe"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: With time programmers are becoming more environmentally conscious and sustainable."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le02ob08aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sustainable"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "able to continue over a period of time, causing little or no damage to the environment"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: With time programmers are becoming more environmentally conscious and sustainable."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le02ob08aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about encapsulation in OOP"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Describe how it works"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a brochure about encapsulation"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Show your brochure to your classmates and teacher"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I can give details about encapsulation and trends in OOP. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can explain briefly the concept of encapsulation and trends."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can talk to a group of co-workers what encapsulation and trends are."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n3le02ob08re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n3le02ob08re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "Hello, everyone, I called this meeting because we need to focus on programming languages. There are different trends and details about encapsulation that we can use taking into account encapsulation as one fundamental OOP concept. </br>By using encapsulation, designers are able to promote the development of programs with reliability, software developers can create organized libraries and other programmers can use them. We can use interface specifications, in this way we could create more readable programs."}, {"time": "37000", "image": "enpe8n3le02ob08re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "There are different advantages of using encapsulation and there are some large libraries created by the programmers. For example we can use this technique to hide data members and members' functions, with this, we can ensure security in our software. </br>We know that OOP trends have been fad by other programmers judging its capabilities and effectiveness by the implementation of Smalltalk. However, the introduction of C++ could allow programmers to improve the object-oriented world. Many software developers realized that there are many other options by using Microsoft to structure their access to a newer operating system."}, {"time": "80000", "image": "enpe8n3le02ob08re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "With time programmers are becoming more environmentally conscious and sustainable, and they established as a trend the possibility to distribute documents electronically, which also led to office automation. Many corporate manuals are kept in the websites so people can update and consult them when necessary. </br>In the last years the use of Internet has evolved and improved communication, therefore, as a company and co-workers we need to implement encapsulation processes in our day-to-day duties. In our case as a trend we can use the benefits of the Internet for internal communication and collaboration in the office, simple processes such as a blog or wikis that can benefit employees and customers' knowledge and keep everyone updated. As follows we can see the impact on customer service sales and revenue."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n3le02ob08re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "L